 MLLMs for the gene task.", "vlm_descriptions": ["SCIENTIFIC_FIGURE\n\nThe image is a multi-panel scientific plot figure with six labeled panels: **a, b, c, d, e, f**. Each panel shows line plots of **Model performance** on the y-axis, with legends for three metrics: **truthfulness** in red with star markers, **structure** in cyan with circular markers, and **average** in blue with circular markers.\n\nPanels:\n- **a**: Model performance vs **Epochs** at 1, 5, 10, 20. Structure remains near 1.0; truthfulness and average increase slightly toward high performance.\n- **b**: Model performance vs **Cut-off length** at 512, 1024, 2048. All metrics remain high and mostly flat, with structure at about 1.0 and truthfulness around 0.95.\n- **c**: Model performance vs **Epochs** at 1, 5, 10. Structure remains near 1.0, while truthfulness decreases from roughly 0.35 to 0.25 and average decreases slightly.\n- **d**: Model performance vs **Epochs** at 1, 5, 10. Structure remains near 1.0; truthfulness rises sharply at epoch 10; average also increases strongly at epoch 10.\n- **e**: Model performance vs **Cut-off length** at 512, 1024, 2048. Structure increases to near 1.0; truthfulness remains low but improves from about 0.1 to 0.3; average rises from about 0.5 to about 0.65.\n- **f**: Model performance vs **Cut-off length** at 512, 1024, 2048. All metrics start near 0 at 512 and improve substantially by 1024 and 2048, with structure reaching near 1.0 and truthfulness near 0.9 at 2048.\n\nNo biological source objects, microscopy images, anatomical structures, molecular structures, or experimental transformations are visible. The figure appears to compare model evaluation metrics across training epochs and cut-off lengths."]}, {"figure_index": 4, "page_no": 15, "caption": "Extended Data Fig. 1: Definition of different evaluators or scorers. For the scorer focusing on truthfulness, we evaluate the matching level of model outputs for the description of gene properties and gene func